<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Birchas HaHodaah [The Blessing of Thanksgiving] — Halachah 2<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">COMPLETE · Based on <span class="lr">LM I:7</span> (<i>V'Aileh HaMishpatim</i>)</span></div>

<div class="sa"><b>Shulchan Aruch text:</b> Four are obligated to give thanks: a sick person who was healed, those who go down to the sea, etc., travelers through wildernesses, and one who was imprisoned. The mnemonic is: <i>"and all who live [v'chol ha'<b>ch</b>a'<b>y</b>'<b>i</b>'<b>m</b>'] shall thank You"</i> etc. (Shulchan Aruch, siman 219).</div>

<div class="sn">Emunah = Miracles = Tefilah = Eretz Yisrael</div>

<div class="p">Based on the teaching "<span class="h">V'Aileh HaMishpatim</span>" which discusses <span class="h">emunah</span> (<span class="lr">LM I:7</span>); see there. For <span class="h">emunah</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">tefilah</span>, the aspect of miracles — that one believes there is One who renews and in whose hand it is to change nature. The essential <span class="h">tefilah</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span>, the aspect of miracles — is only in <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, etc. Therefore, when Avraham damaged in <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> by saying <span class="v">"how shall I know?"</span> — through this, Yaakov and his sons descended into the exile of Egypt. For the essential exile is because of the deficiency of <span class="h">emunah</span>, etc. The essential <span class="h">ge'ulah</span> [redemption] is through <span class="h">emunah</span>, in the aspect of: <span class="v">"you shall come, you shall gaze from the peak of Amanah"</span> etc. (Shir HaShirim 4). But to merit <span class="h">emunah</span>, one must attain truth — for <span class="mx">"when <i>tzedek</i> joins with <i>emes</i>, it becomes <i>emunah</i>."</span> The essential truth is merited only through drawing close to true <span class="h">tzadikim</span> — by receiving their counsel, for they are the aspect of <span class="mx">"a faithful offspring — entirely seed of truth,"</span> the aspect of the 613 counsels of the Torah, etc.</div>

<div class="p">Through the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, one merits being saved from the counsel of the wicked, which is the aspect of adultery, etc. — for <span class="h">tzitzis</span> is a protection from adultery. Therefore through <span class="h">tzitzis</span> one merits receiving counsel from the <span class="h">tzadikim</span>, who are the aspect of guarding the <span class="h">bris</span>, the aspect of <span class="mx">"a faithful offspring — entirely seed of truth."</span> Through this one merits <span class="h">emunah</span>, as mentioned above. Through this the <span class="h">ge'ulah</span> will come, etc., as above; see there.</div>

<div class="sn">The Four Who Give Thanks Reveal Emunah and Defeat the Four Exiles</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of <span class="h">Birchas HaHodaos HaNissim</span> [blessings of thanksgiving for miracles]. One must give thanks and bless Hashem for the miracles — in order to reveal <span class="h">emunah</span> in the world, to know and make known that Hashem governs the world and in His mercy changed nature and performed a miracle for him. This is the essential aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as above. For miracles, the aspect of <span class="h">tefilah</span>, are the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as above.</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the four who must give thanks. When a miracle is performed and one thanks Hashem for it — and through this <span class="h">emunah</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">tefilah</span>, is revealed, as above — through this the <span class="h">ge'ulah</span> will come and one merits leaving the exile of the four kingdoms. For the essential exile is because of the deficiency of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as above. Therefore they are four who must give thanks — corresponding to the four exiles. For through the four who must give thanks, all four exiles are subdued and nullified. For the essential exile is through the deficiency of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as above. Through the four who must give thanks — through the thanksgiving for miracles — <span class="h">emunah</span> is revealed, as above, through which the <span class="h">ge'ulah</span> will come, as above.</div>

<div class="p">For <span class="h">emunah</span> is the aspect of the <span class="h">daled</span> of <span class="v">"Echad"</span> [in <span class="h">Krias Shma</span>]. Therefore the essential <span class="h">emunah</span> is through the <span class="h">tzadik</span>, who is the aspect of truth, as above. For the <span class="h">tzadik</span> is the <span class="h">kotz</span> [serif] of the letter <span class="h">daled</span>, as brought in the Tikunim (Tikun 21, daf 55b). The essential sustaining of <span class="h">emunah</span> — which is the <span class="h">daled</span> of <span class="v">"Echad"</span> — is through the <span class="h">tzadik</span>, who is the aspect of <span class="mx">"a faithful offspring — entirely seed of truth,"</span> as above. Therefore the <span class="h">tzadik</span> is the <span class="h">kotz</span> of the letter <span class="h">daled</span>, as above.</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the four <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, through which one merits drawing close to the <span class="h">tzadik</span> and meriting <span class="h">emunah</span>, as above. Through the four <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, one merits the closeness of the <span class="h">tzadik</span> — who is the <span class="h">kotz</span> of the letter <span class="h">daled</span>, the aspect of <span class="mx">"a faithful offspring — entirely seed of truth"</span> — through whom the essential sustaining of <span class="h">emunah</span> is accomplished, as above. Through <span class="h">emunah</span>, one merits <span class="h">ge'ulah</span> and leaves the four exiles, as above. This is the aspect of the four who must give thanks — four specifically, as above.</div>

<div class="sn">Yetzias Mitzrayim: All Four in One</div>

<div class="p">For all the four who must give thanks are in the aspect of <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span>. The exile of Egypt came about through the damage of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as above, in the above teaching; see there. Likewise all four exiles are called by the name "Mitzrayim," and they all come through the damage of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as above. <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span> — the aspect of miracles, the aspect of <span class="h">tefilah</span>, <span class="h">emunah</span> — this is the aspect of the four who must give thanks. Through the thanksgiving, the aspect of <span class="h">tefilah</span>, one publicizes and reveals the miracle, the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as above. This is the aspect of <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span> — for the essential <span class="h">ge'ulah</span> is through <span class="h">emunah</span>, in the aspect of: <span class="v">"and they believed in Hashem and in Moshe His servant"</span> (Shemos 14), as above.</div>

<div class="p">For at the time of <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span>, Israel experienced all four above-mentioned aspects of the four who must give thanks. They left the exile and captivity of Egypt — this is the aspect of one who was imprisoned and was released. They were also saved from the illness of Egypt, as it says (Shemos 15): <span class="v">"all the disease that I placed upon Egypt I shall not place upon you, for I am Hashem your healer"</span> — this is the aspect of the miracle and thanksgiving of one who was sick and was healed. They were also sea-travelers, and Hashem performed for them the great miracle of the splitting of the <span class="h">Yam Suf</span>. And they were also wilderness-travelers. Thus at the time of <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span>, Israel experienced all four miracles of the four who must give thanks.</div>

<div class="sn">Tzitzis and Yetzias Mitzrayim</div>

<div class="p">The essential <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span> and splitting of the <span class="h">Yam Suf</span> was through the aspect of <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, in the aspect of: <span class="v">"I carried you on the wings of eagles"</span> — <span class="mx">"this refers to the wings of a mitzvah"</span> (see Zohar, Yisro 93a and Ohr HaChamah there, and Tikun 10, 25b) — the aspect of <span class="h">tzitzis</span>. The splitting of the <span class="h">Yam Suf</span> is likewise stated in the Midrash (Yalkut Shimoni, Shemos 14, #234): it was in the merit of the four corners — the sea saw the merit of the four corners of <span class="h">tzitzis</span> and split before them. For the essential revelation of miracles — which are the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span>, <span class="h">tefilah</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span> — is through the aspect of the four <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, as above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span> is mentioned in the <span class="h">parshah</span> of <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, and we recite the <span class="h">parshah</span> of <span class="h">tzitzis</span> every day in <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> in order to mention <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span> every day. At first glance it is difficult: why was the <span class="h">parshah</span> of <span class="h">tzitzis</span> specifically chosen? There are many <span class="h">parshiyos</span> in the Torah that mention <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span>! And also, why was the <span class="h">parshah</span> of <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, which is the remembrance of <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span>, placed adjacent to <span class="h">Krias Shma</span>?</div>

<div class="p">But the essential <span class="h">emunah</span> that we receive through <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> is only through the aspect of <span class="h">tzitzis</span>. Through <span class="h">tzitzis</span> one merits the closeness of the <span class="h">tzadik</span>, through whom the essential <span class="h">emunah</span> is accomplished. This is the aspect of <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span>, as above — for the essential <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span>, is through <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, as above. Therefore we recite specifically the <span class="h">parshah</span> of <span class="h">tzitzis</span> for the remembrance of <span class="h">Yetzias Mitzrayim</span>, and we place it adjacent to <span class="h">Krias Shma</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as above.</div>

<div class="sn">Thanking Before Ten, Two of Them Torah Scholars</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of: <span class="mx">"one must give thanks before ten, two of whom are Torah scholars."</span> For wherever there are ten, the <span class="h">Shechinah</span> rests. The <span class="h">Shechinah</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as is known. Therefore two of them must be Torah scholars — for the essential revelation of <span class="h">emunah</span> is through the <span class="h">Rabbonan</span> who are occupied in Torah, from whom one receives holy counsel, the aspect of the 613 counsels of the Torah, the aspect of <span class="mx">"a faithful offspring — entirely seed of truth,"</span> the aspect of the <span class="h">tzadikim</span> of the generation through whom the essential sustaining of <span class="h">emunah</span> is accomplished. Therefore two of them must be Torah scholars — for the essential publicizing of the miracle, which is the revelation of <span class="h">emunah</span>, is through the <span class="h">talmidai chachamim</span> specifically, as above.</div>

<div class="sn">HaGomel at the Torah Reading; Blessing at the Place of the Miracle</div>

<div class="p">Therefore the custom is to recite <span class="h">Birchas HaGomel</span> at the time of the Torah reading — for the essential revelation of miracles is through <span class="h">Toras Emes</span>, through the 613 counsels of the Torah, etc., as above in the above teaching; see there.</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of what one blesses when coming to a place where a miracle was done for him: <span class="v">"Blessed is He who performed a miracle for me in this place."</span> One must mention the aspect of "place" — for the essential term <span class="h">makom</span> [place] refers to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, which is called <span class="h">makom</span>, as it says (Beraishis 28): <span class="v">"he encountered the place"</span>; in the aspect of <span class="v">"to the place that G-d told him"</span> (ibid. 22). For Hashem is called <span class="h">Makom</span>, as our Sages say: <span class="mx">"He is the Place of the world."</span> The essential revelation of His G-dliness is in <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> — for <span class="mx">"one who dwells in Eretz Yisrael is like one who has a G-d."</span> Therefore <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is called <span class="h">makom</span>. And there in <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is the essential revelation of miracles, as above. Therefore one must bless: "Blessed is He who performed a miracle for me <b>in this place</b>" — <span class="h">b'makom</span> specifically. For the essential miracle is through the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, which is called <span class="h">makom</span> — because the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> was drawn here. All miracles are drawn from <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, where miracles are in their essence — for <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is the aspect of miracles, the aspect of <span class="h">tefilah</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span>, as above.</div>

<div class="p" style="font-style:italic;color:var(--accent)">Halachah 3 is included in Hilchos Birchas HaRaiach, Halachah 1.<br>Halachah 4 is included in Hilchos Birchas HaRaiach, Halachah 4.</div>

<div class="cn">✦ End of Halachah 2 — Birchas HaHodaah [The Blessing of Thanksgiving] ✦<br><i>Na Nach Nachma Nachman May'Uman</i></div>

